WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.800
A paying agent reads an x402 offer
and sends funds to the address it names.

00:04.800 --> 00:08.400
A chain receipt proves payment,
but not seller authorization.

00:12.000 --> 00:18.800
In a read-only sweep of Circle’s marketplace, twenty listings
from three sellers returned payout addresses different from the catalog.

00:18.800 --> 00:22.800
A difference is not fraud.
It is a verification problem.

00:24.000 --> 00:29.200
Purser asks the seller to sign the address
and publish an identity key on its own domain.

00:29.200 --> 00:31.500
The buyer checks that evidence before signing.

00:36.000 --> 00:41.200
Twenty authorization scenarios
and twenty local-chain execution scenarios pass.

00:41.200 --> 00:47.300
The model can propose, but payment controls decide.
These are local experiments, not Arc settlement.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.400
One QuickNode testnet call cost 0.0001 USDC.
Its answer passed a public node check.

00:53.400 --> 00:58.900
The Arc batch confirms the debit and credit.
Seller authorization remains unconfirmed: one human exception.
